      "content": "The Eurostar's luggage policy is quite straightforward, though it's always best to check the official website for the most current details before you go. Generally, you are allowed two pieces of hand luggage, plus a small personal item, but the weight limits can vary depending on your ticket class. For most standard fares, you should be able to bring your suitcases onto the train, and you usually don't need to check them in beforehand at the station, but you do need to be mindful of the size and weight restrictions. It's a good idea to keep your most valuable items with you, just in case.",
